      "category": "fsm",
      "family": "request_delay",
      "split": "development",
      "spec": "Implement module request_delay(input clk, input rst_n, input din, output q). Use rising clock edges, asynchronous active-low reset, and Moore outputs. Initially idle with q=0. In idle, a sampled din=1 accepts a request. q remains 0 on that accepting edge, then is 1 for exactly the following clock cycle, regardless of din. At the next edge q returns to 0 and enters cooldown. In cooldown, remain there while din=1; an edge with din=0 returns to idle. The edge returning to idle does not accept a request.",
